{"id": "EUVD-2026-103573", "enisaUuid": "3f9d3c08-e55f-3c83-82ce-d7e0be90226b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ngpio: cdev: fix kernel stack leak to user-space in error path\n\nIf we fail to acquire the GPIO chip guard in gpio_desc_to_lineinfo(), we\nreturn immediately before zeroing the info struct we'll end up passing\nto the user-space later in lineinfo_get_v1(). This may leak the kernel\nstack contents. Make gpio_desc_to_lineinfo() return int so that the\n-ENODEV returned on failure to acquire the guard can be propagated to\nthe callers.\n\nWhile not strictly necessary: move the memset() before trying to acquire\nthe SRCU read lock too for good measure.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:17:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:21:10", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8460ee5216ab9a38263b01dca4b0a27e083f70f3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cf3d043582e106a0e57002bec8a6de8929ba3e1c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/60a466f231905cd96ae6f0f3c44a710c97873dac", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1feb5d39b05afd902ed9fc902ec5b15be03a4bdb"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98528", "GHSA-2259-3wph-4x6g"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0112ee41-a546-3002-8b41-9c90784e362e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "06eca1cc-a6b3-3c5a-a5e2-a760897405e1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "2a4033fb-a75e-3d02-886a-e55cb88b0db4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d83cee3d2bb131c7fca7e19f1e33dc7530fd7083 <1feb5d39b05afd902ed9fc902ec5b15be03a4bdb"}, {"id": "89f25d39-fb45-31de-b8f9-df4c70b3af9f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "d90c2189-99c6-3d5c-ae3b-e2c9e1db5673", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d83cee3d2bb131c7fca7e19f1e33dc7530fd7083 <8460ee5216ab9a38263b01dca4b0a27e083f70f3"}, {"id": "dc5be392-cf73-3433-b9ac-7dd3f8fa2ea5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.9"}, {"id": "e56ae6a8-9b19-33ee-bb32-0ea1fe69d7f4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "edc0a3d2-4d21-397c-928f-a0fe4a56489e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d83cee3d2bb131c7fca7e19f1e33dc7530fd7083 <cf3d043582e106a0e57002bec8a6de8929ba3e1c"}, {"id": "f9429ba3-e628-32d4-a524-030e1032e6c2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "fec3f9d5-a57b-3cdd-bd15-ff274f4309e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d83cee3d2bb131c7fca7e19f1e33dc7530fd7083 <60a466f231905cd96ae6f0f3c44a710c97873dac"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2de3b8fd-f8f0-3c6d-a8f7-508a42add834", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}